      "editorial": {
        "en": {
          "why_it_matters": "This is stronger than a generic symphonic-tribute package because several people onstage carry the music through direct living relationships: Melvin Seals and Jacklyn LaBranch come from the Jerry Garcia Band world, while Grahame Lesh and Tom Hamilton connect the material to later branches of the Dead family and improvisational scene. Putting that lineage in front of the National Symphony Orchestra changes the scale without replacing the groove-based core that made Garcia's live language work.",
          "trip_verdict": "Actively make room for the Wolf Trap night if the Dead/Garcia thread matters. The NSO and the lineage-heavy featured band make this a particularly good DMV edition of the project, while the same symphonic concept is touring several cities with other orchestras, so there is no need to treat this stop as a singular once-only event.",
